# Culvert appliance: the DRM device nodes are root-only.
#
# vmwgfx (the VMware SVGA display driver the ESXi console uses) carries open
# HIGH CVEs reached through DRM ioctls (CVE-2026-80700: a crafted atomic commit
# on a configured CRTC; CVE-2026-80702: resource release/unbind). The driver
# cannot be denied without losing the console, so the prerequisite is removed
# instead: nothing on the appliance draws through DRM except plymouth, which
# runs as root, and the appliance console renders on a text VT. Ubuntu's
# default gives card* to group video (0660) and renderD* to group render, and
# logind's uaccess tag grants a local console session an ACL on them. This
# rule makes every DRM node root:root 0600 and drops the uaccess tag, so no
# unprivileged user — and no container, which gets no /dev/dri anyway — can
# open one. It sorts before 73-seat-late.rules, where uaccess is applied.
SUBSYSTEM=="drm", KERNEL=="card[0-9]*|renderD[0-9]*|controlD[0-9]*", GROUP="root", MODE="0600", TAG-="uaccess"
